# ============================ VinaX environment ============================
# Frontend (Vite). PUBLIC — never put secrets in VITE_* variables.
# Optional overrides; the app works with none of these set.
# VITE_API_BASES=https://saavn.dev/api,https://saavn.sumit.co/api
# VITE_APP_NAME=VinaX

# ------- Server-side secrets (Cloudflare WORKER `vinax-api`) -------
# Set with: npx wrangler secret put <NAME> --config worker/wrangler.toml
# (or Workers dashboard -> vinax-api -> Settings -> Variables & Secrets).
# They live on the Worker, never on Pages, and never reach the client.
# This file documents names only — real values belong in Cloudflare (or a local
# worker/.dev.vars for `npm run dev` in backend/, which is gitignored).
#
# AI keys — 10.3: ONE key per provider. Each key opens its provider's whole
# free catalogue (listed live by functions/_lib/catalog.ts and selectable model
# by model in VinaX AI), and the feature lanes in functions/_lib/ai.ts sign
# with the key of their provider. After setting them, open the admin AI Lab
# and bench each provider.
#
# 10.3 — the PRIMARY names are NVIDIA_API_KEY, OPENROUTER_API_KEY,
# GROQ_API_KEY and GEMINI_API_KEY. Each falls back to its previous name
# (VINAX_NVIDIA_API_KEY, VINAX_OPENROUTER_API_KEY, VINAX_GROQ_API_KEY,
# VINAX_GGL_GEMINI_API_KEY) while the primary is unset, so the live Worker
# keeps working during the switch; the admin env checklist says when a
# previous name is the one in use. Set the new name, then delete the old one.
# Each key also opens that provider's FREE media models (image generation,
# speech, transcription, music, embeddings) and free non-web tools (code
# execution) — see GET /api/aimodels. The only web tools are Gemini's own
# search grounding and the web search key below.
#
# NVIDIA_API_KEY                 NVIDIA (nvapi-...) — account-scoped: this one
#                                key signs every NVIDIA lane (dj, chat, deep,
#                                fast, home, search, pro, mini, vision,
#                                vision90), the NVIDIA embeddings and the image
#                                endpoint, and opens NVIDIA's free catalogue.
#                                It replaces every per-model NVIDIA secret of
#                                the 2026-09-09 generation.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY             OpenRouter — the router lane. Only models the
#                                provider prices at zero in BOTH directions are
#                                ever offered, so this key cannot run up a bill
#                                (a media model must also list its output price
#                                as zero, or be a :free variant)
# GROQ_API_KEY                   Groq (gsk_...) — the scholar lane: music
#                                knowledge · lyrics · LIVE voice · TTS ·
#                                transcription · code execution, and its free
#                                chat catalogue
# GEMINI_API_KEY                 Gemini — the maestro (flagship) lane: leads
#                                the AI DJ, the Queue Builder, AI Playlist,
#                                song ranking and the Home builder, and Auto in
#                                VinaX AI whenever this key is set; also its
#                                free catalogue (a model whose free-tier limit
#                                is 0 for this key is left out for a day) and
#                                the second embeddings engine.
#                                Create the key in the provider's AI studio
#                                and set it with `wrangler secret put`; never
#                                paste it into chat, a ticket, a VITE_*
#                                variable — or into VINAX_MAESTRO_MODEL.
#                                A 429 (quota) cools the model for a while and
#                                the next lane answers.
# VINAX_MAESTRO_MODEL            optional plain var (not a secret): a model
#                                NAME — a lowercase slug exactly as the
#                                provider publishes it — that replaces the
#                                maestro lane's pinned model when the provider
#                                publishes a newer one. Never the key: a value
#                                that looks like a key, or is not a slug, is
#                                ignored (logged once per isolate) and the pin
#                                is used, and log lines print `[masked]` for a
#                                key-shaped model name (8.1; before that a key
#                                pasted here was sent as the model name and
#                                printed in the request log).
#
# Web search in VinaX AI (11.8) — NOT an AI key (the four above are the only
# ones), so it is not on any lane:
#   SERPER_API_KEY       Serper (google.serper.dev) API key. Used only on a chat
#                        turn about current events that Gemini's own search
#                        grounding does not answer. Unset = no web search.
#                        The free allowance is a ONE-TIME 2,500 queries.
#                        Local: put `SERPER_API_KEY=...` in worker/.dev.vars
#                        (gitignored) for `npm run dev`.
#   SERPER_DAILY_LIMIT   plain var in worker/wrangler.toml [vars] (default 80):
#                        searches allowed per UTC day; cached repeats are free.
#
# NVIDIA_BASE_URL optional DEFAULT endpoint override (lanes without a LANE_BASE pin)
#
# Database (14.0) — one hosted project; the Worker is its only client. Apply
# backend/supabase/schema.sql in the project's SQL editor once (idempotent),
# then set these two. Without them every data feature answers its
# "not configured" shape and the console's data pages show their setup card.
# See docs/database.md.
#   SUPABASE_URL                 https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#   SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY    the project's service-role key (bypasses
#                                row-level security; never the anon key,
#                                never in the frontend)
#
# Scheduled jobs run on the Worker's own Cron Trigger (worker/wrangler.toml
# [triggers]); no secret is needed for them. Optional:
#   CRON_SECRET            lets `POST /api/cron/run { job }` be called with the
#                          header x-cron-secret from outside the console (the
#                          owner token works too). Unset = owner token only.
#
# Admin console (…/admin — gates every /api/admin endpoint):
#   ADMIN_LOGIN_PASSWORD   long random secret
#
# Web push (VAPID keypair, generate once and keep):
#   VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY       base64url, 65-byte uncompressed P-256 point
#   VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY      base64url, 32-byte P-256 scalar
#   VAPID_SUBJECT          mailto:owner@example.com
#
# Device identity and request hashing:
#   DEVICE_ID_SECRET       REQUIRED for the data features: signs the device
#                          ids /api/events and /api/username issue and verify
#                          (worker/functions/_lib/identity.ts), and derives a
#                          device's server id from its install id. Set a long
#                          random secret; changing it gives every device a new
#                          identity. TELEMETRY_PEPPER is read as a fallback
#                          name while this is unset.
#   TELEMETRY_PEPPER       HMAC pepper that seeds the rate-limiter key hash
#                          (in isolate memory and in the rate-limit binding
#                          keys), so plaintext IPs are never kept. Set a long
#                          random secret.
#
# Optional Google sign-in (12.2):
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID       plain var in worker/wrangler.toml [vars]: the public
#                          web OAuth client id of the push/sign-in project.
#   AUTH_SECRET            long random secret that signs sign-in sessions.
#                          Falls back to DEVICE_ID_SECRET when unset; set a
#                          dedicated one so they can be rotated separately.
#
# Not secrets and not set here (7.2.0) — listed so nobody looks for them:
#   RATE_LIMIT_10 / RATE_LIMIT_30 / RATE_LIMIT_60 / RATE_LIMIT_300,
#   ADMIN_AUTH_FAILS       Workers Rate Limiting bindings declared in
#                          worker/wrangler.toml. Without them (local dev,
#                          tests) limits are per-isolate memory only.
#
# Optional integrations:
#   GITHUB_REPO            owner/repo used by the APK release endpoint
#   GITHUB_TOKEN           optional; raises GitHub API rate limits

# Native Android background push (FCM) — optional; enables notifications
# even when the app is fully closed. See docs/fcm-push-setup.md.
#   FCM_SERVICE_ACCOUNT   Firebase service-account JSON (whole file, as a string)
